<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n108159" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποβρύχιος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ῠχ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>under water,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν δ᾽ ἄνεμος . . καὶ κῦμα θαλάσσης
					θῆκαν ὑποβρυχίην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Hom.</u>
					33.12
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποβρύχιον . . φέρων</span> (sc.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν ἵππον</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.189
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. θάνατοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Cat.Cod.Astr.</u>
					2.161
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ Ἑλλὰς ὑ. φερομένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aristid.
					<u>Or.</u>
					23(42).46
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>below the surface,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποβρύχιαι συμπεριφέρονται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phdr.</u>
					248a
				</span></i>
			; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιπολάζων,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Dips.</u>
				3
			</span></i>; <i>deep-seated,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκπυήσιες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Art.</u>
					12
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑ. πυρετός</span> a
			<i>hidden</i> fever, one <i>that shows itself by degrees,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Epid.</u>
				1.25
			</span></i> (so Littré with <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				9.560
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρχεται μαλακῶς καὶ
			ὑποβρύχια</span> [Adv.] codd., Kühl.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρετοὶ -ιοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>SD</u>
					2.9
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀφθαλμῶν ὑ. πόνος</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				1.2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῦρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>SA</u>
					2.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>deep,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θάλασσα, βυσσός,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				1.49
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				5.159
			</span></i>.—Cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βρύχιος,
			περιβρύχιος.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑποβρυχώμενος</span>
			, of oxen, <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Merc.</u>
				116
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
